      {
        "id": 146698,
        "name": "payprplayn",
        "username": "payprplayn",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-08T20:32:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Donner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/48/1903_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Donner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Go, Bots! is unlimited and allows your bots to repeat actions you can normally take once each turn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>and later</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Donner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/48/1903_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Donner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Raptor Bot: The strongest attacker at 5 dice, 1 automiss. &nbsp;Great for reconfiguration combos from Swift Bot. &nbsp;<strong>If left alone, can make up to 3 attacks in a round!</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>(emphasis mine)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Is this a change?&nbsp; My initial reading of the powers as well as (at one point, though I haven't looked in a while) the F.A.Q. seemed to indicate that while Go Bots! is unlimited, individual bot actions are not.&nbsp;Thus, while unity can use Go Bots! twice (or more)&nbsp;in a round (say, to have Raptor bot aim and then attack, or to have two different bots sprint), raptor bot still can't attack twice in a single round, nor can turret bot dodge twice, etc.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:24:40.206Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
